    "method": "dem-ridge",
    "description": "Crest line of the inner rampart, derived from the committed 1 m LiDAR DEM (dem_core.tif). Transects are cast every 1.0 m along a smoothed copy of the RAÄ/KMR site-extent polygon, running from 5.0 m outside to 25.0 m inside it; each transect's height profile is detrended against a 24.0 m moving average and the maximum of that residual is taken as the bank crest (the fort interior stands higher than the rampart, so an undetrended maximum would walk inland). A circular median over 25.0 m of those first picks guides a second pass restricted to ±5.0 m around it, so the entrance gaps — where there is no bank to find — follow the neighbouring crest instead of wandering. The result is smoothed over 9.0 m and densified to 0.5 m. The line is measured; the palisade drawn on it is conjecture.",
